    <!-- THE REAL POLISH TRANSLATION — batch 1 of 3 (#1387).

         `values-pl/strings.xml` is NOT this file and never was: it holds the
         Ukrainian Material3 overrides that keep TalkBack coherent on a Polish
         device (#371, #1385). Its guard (`scripts/tests/test_locale_overrides.py`)
         still requires every value there to equal Ukrainian, and the keys that
         moved here were removed from it — a key may live in exactly one file of
         the `pl` qualifier.

         #1387 is the first of three batches (library / shelves / saved). The
         Polish text is complete for the surfaces that reference it; the other
         batches append their own keys to this same file, which is why they go
         one after another. Until the LAST batch adds `pl` to
         `AppLocale.SYSTEM_FOLLOWS` (and to the interface-language screen), a
         Polish-system device keeps the coherent Ukrainian UI: a partly
         translated language shown to the listener is exactly the #1385 defect.

         Rules this file keeps (and `PolishLibraryBatchGuardTest` enforces):
         * every key the library/shelves/saved sources reference has a value
           here — a missing one would silently fall back to Ukrainian;
         * no value is a copy of the Ukrainian one (no Cyrillic letters);
         * every format placeholder (`%1$s`, `%2$d`, `%%`) matches the
           Ukrainian source, so `String.format` cannot throw at runtime. -->

